00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:30.440
<i>Chiga Teruko</i>

00:08:28.270 --> 00:08:30.440
<i>Youngest Triplet Maid</i>

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:30.440
That was a lie.

00:08:31.360 --> 00:08:33.240
Why are you here?

00:08:33.650 --> 00:08:36.700
No reason. It was simply inevitable.

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:38.580
What are you talking about?

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:42.370
Never mind. Just a little nonsense.

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:45.880
That was my line. Again.

00:08:48.090 --> 00:08:49.420
Thank you.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:10.820
I knew it. This was the end of me.

00:09:11.530 --> 00:09:14.240
I had a hunch this was how it would go down.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:17.870
It was a shame Teruko had to get mixed up in it...

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:21.410
But this was mostly what I'd had in mind.

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:24.460
I'd only had one goal.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.830
To keep Kunagisa out of it.

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:31.170
Nothing else mattered.

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.420
Nothing at all.

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:35.760
Apathy. Disinterest.

00:09:36.590 --> 00:09:39.430
I'd long ago forgotten being born.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:42.680
I'd never known what it felt like to be alive.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:46.350
Teruko's body, leaning against me.

00:09:47.390 --> 00:09:49.560
My ankle, throbbing.

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:53.730
My thoughts paralyzed. My values shattering.

00:09:54.490 --> 00:09:57.910
My logic melting. My morals crumbling.

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:00.070
Kanami's head.

00:10:01.030 --> 00:10:02.450
Akane's head.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:04.620
The truth.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:06.000
The culprit.

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:08.120
The murderer.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:10.210
The killer.

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:13.420
Tearing everything apart.

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:18.220
But nothing mattered now.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:20.180
I forgave everything.

00:10:21.850 --> 00:10:22.510
So...

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:24.770
So pull that trigger.

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:26.730
And finish this.

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:30.860
Ii-chan!

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:48.580
How...?

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:54.880
Climbing that spiral staircase was impossible,
unless someone was with her.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:57.010
She couldn't be here.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:10:59.380
Despite that...

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:02.680
Despite that, when Kunagisa heard the gunshot...

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:05.510
Even though it must have been horrific...

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:11.650
Even though the pain of it might literally have killed her...

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:14.270
Forcing her legs to stand.

00:11:14.940 --> 00:11:16.900
Cracking a whip on her terrified soul.

00:11:17.990 --> 00:11:20.400
Her mind too fragile to live.

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:24.990
Past pain like infinite hell.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:27.700
She came for me.

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:32.540
Not caring how, no matter what.

00:11:33.250 --> 00:11:36.000
Kunagisa Tomo came for me.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:39.050
Why?

00:11:40.170 --> 00:11:41.220
Why do you...?

00:11:45.850 --> 00:11:50.270
Good! You're safe, Ii-chan.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:54.650
I...I really...

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:59.150
I love her.

00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:05.910
So please. Don't.

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:30.980
Not everything I'd hoped for...

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:39.610
But for a man like you to admit something
like that...I guess that's enough for one day.

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:39.820
<i>Sonoyama Akane</i>

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:39.820
<i>Genius - Seven Fools</i>

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:39.690
Smaller boxes so I
need a different am
ount of text to cover
everything up this t

00:12:40.690 --> 00:12:43.950
You wouldn't admit that last night.

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:59.000
2nd Floor, Kunagisa Tomo's Room

00:12:55.370 --> 00:12:59.000
Jeez, look at this bruise, Ii-chan!

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:05.430
Akane was on the karate team in high school, you know.

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:09.470
I...may have heard something along those lines.

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:12.520
She went all the way to the nationals.

00:13:12.810 --> 00:13:13.810
Wish you'd said.

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:22.030
Meanwhile, Akane's injuries were a broken arm...

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:28.120
And that first kick had broken four ribs, too.

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:30.240
As for Teruko...

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:36.330
When the gun went off, I thought she'd been shot in the back...

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:39.250
Apparently the bullet didn't even hit her.

00:13:39.880 --> 00:13:42.500
She'd thrown herself out of the way.

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:45.970
And then pretended she was dead.

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:49.510
Oh, that's not quite right...

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:53.720
I bet Teruko was being your shield.

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:54.520
Shield?

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:58.230
Teruko's maid uniform is bulletproof.

00:13:58.230 --> 00:13:59.400
Bulletproof...?

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:03.030
Right...

00:14:03.980 --> 00:14:06.950
So why is Teruko so strong?

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:11.030
Teruko is primarily Miss Ilia's bodyguard.

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:17.750
I mean, have you ever seen her working with me and Akari?

00:14:19.170 --> 00:14:21.920
But I'm surprised she saved you.

00:14:22.880 --> 00:14:28.010
I'm sure you noticed, but she's not the caring type.

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:33.970
Saving you is one thing, but actually putting herself in harm's way?

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:37.100
The mind boggles.

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:42.270
Your back seems OK.

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:46.280
And your hips...you didn't hit your head, right?

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:50.660
All right, then you're all done!

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:53.870
Right! Let's go, Ii-chan!

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:56.620
But do my hair first.

00:14:57.910 --> 00:14:59.750
You don't like it?

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:02.960
Feels like it's pulling on me!

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:06.710
I like it better with just one or two.

00:15:08.340 --> 00:15:09.380
It's cute, though.

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:22.310
Nonsense, right?

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:27.900
Blot this alll of

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:27.900
4444

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:27.900
Another line

00:15:25.900 --> 00:15:27.900
<i>Killer</i>

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:32.320
Then...let's get going.

00:15:33.490 --> 00:15:35.910
What <i>is</i> all this?

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:37.410
I'll explain.

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:42.040
The killer is Sonoyama Akane, member of ER3's Seven Fools.

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:46.710
And her accomplice was Sakaki Shinya, Ibuki Kanami's assistant.

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:49.800
And?

00:15:50.130 --> 00:15:51.050
That's it.

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:53.180
Make this last at least half an hour.

00:15:55.220 --> 00:16:01.690
First, explain...how was Sonoyama there at all?

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:03.690
Simple enough.

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:06.440
Yayoi ran out of the dining room.

00:16:06.900 --> 00:16:15.070
Knowing she would be alone, Akane waited for her in her room. To kill her.

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:21.120
Wasn't Sonoyama killed? In the locked storeroom?

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:27.130
If a body is beheaded, assume someone's
switched places. Iron rule of mystery novels.

00:16:27.340 --> 00:16:31.630
Um...hang on, let me think.

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:39.890
Lord this 1
is tiny yo!

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:39.890
<i>Mansion's
Head Maid</i>

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:39.890
<i>Handa Rei</i>

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:40.390
I give up.

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:42.770
Was it really just a trick?

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:45.230
Yes. A simple body swap.

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:50.820
Kunagisa's computers were smashed, right?
But none of us could have done that.

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:54.280
We were all watching each other the whole time.

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:56.620
If nobody here could do it...

00:16:57.820 --> 00:16:59.740
Then someone <i>not</i> here must have.

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:03.160
Logical deduction.

00:17:03.790 --> 00:17:06.380
Which brings us to the key to everything...

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:10.800
Ibuki Kanami.

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:16.550
A body in a sleeping bag can be buried without getting dirty.

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:18.050
Strange, isn't it?

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:23.980
When we buried Kanami, Shinya just showed up with a sleeping bag.

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:28.480
Did he get it from the mansion? I assumed as much.

00:17:29.060 --> 00:17:32.530
I thought Ilia had provided it for the burial.

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:39.030
But then when it was Akane's turn, Hikari brought a stretcher.

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:45.080
If you have sleeping bags, why would you
provide one the first time, and not the second?

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:46.580
It didn't add up.

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:50.840
It makes more sense if that was Shinya's sleeping bag.

00:17:51.590 --> 00:17:58.720
Because he knew he'd need a coffin. Something
to keep the body clean. Only reason he'd have one.

00:17:59.090 --> 00:18:02.220
So they...reused the body?

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:10.360
Yes. Akane and Shinya killed Ibuki Kanami, and then
used her body to create the illusion of a second murder.

00:18:11.860 --> 00:18:14.320
But there was blood in the storeroom.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:18.990
If that body was a day old, how would it bleed?

00:18:18.990 --> 00:18:23.490
We had no way of telling if that blood was Akane's.

00:18:23.990 --> 00:18:25.620
The police could have.

00:18:25.910 --> 00:18:30.380
If we'd called the police, this would never have been a mystery at all.

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:35.630
But Ilia wouldn't call the police; she has reasons not to.

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:43.890
If they knew that, then Akane could assume no
matter what she did, no police would ever come.

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:50.900
Likewise, if the police were here, they'd
have known that body was a day old.

00:18:51.810 --> 00:18:54.860
They dressed the body up?

00:18:54.860 --> 00:19:02.820
Yes; the reason Akane called Hikari late that night
was to show what clothes Akane was wearing.

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:09.370
When Hikari visited the room, Kanami's body was already there.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:14.840
The door opens inwards, so it was easy to hide the body behind the door.

00:19:17.630 --> 00:19:20.430
That was probably their biggest risk.

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:23.680
But they needed to take that risk.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:29.810
It was the clothes that made us so certain that body was Akane.

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:36.320
And it placed the time of the murder at night,
when her accomplice had an airtight alibi.

00:19:37.480 --> 00:19:40.950
Shinya had spent that night drinking with Maki.

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:41.950
Smaller boxes so I
need a different am
ount of text to cover
everything up this t

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:41.950
<i>Himena Maki</i>

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:41.950
<i>Genius Fortune Teller</i>

00:19:43.620 --> 00:19:46.540
And this is why she smashed Kunagisa's computers.

00:19:47.240 --> 00:19:51.670
We'd taken photos Kanami's body with a digital
camera, and she didn't want us having those.

00:19:52.420 --> 00:20:00.050
If we compared those images to the body in the store room,
there was a chance we'd notice they were the same.

00:20:00.340 --> 00:20:03.050
But why do any of that?

00:20:03.050 --> 00:20:06.390
If she was murdered, nobody would be looking out for her.

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:10.810
She'd be invisible; she could flee beyond
the reach of our thoughts and deductions.

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:14.940
It made it easy for her to destroy Kunagisa's computers.

00:20:15.270 --> 00:20:18.690
And easier to kill someone else, to commit a fourth crime.

00:20:19.230 --> 00:20:21.490
But here we'd have to ask Shinya or Akane --

00:20:21.490 --> 00:20:23.450
She was going to kill everybody.

00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:26.370
Every last one of you.

00:20:26.870 --> 00:20:30.620
But to do that, she had to take herself out of the group.

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:35.040
Akane made it out easily!

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:38.460
Can't believe she didn't manage to kill anyone.

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:43.220
I had her pegged for at least half.

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:46.220
Would you like to explain the rest?

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:48.720
No, you do it.

00:20:49.180 --> 00:20:52.230
That's your role here. Your job.

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:58.270
So, the first locked room...I don't need to explain this, do I?

00:20:59.020 --> 00:21:01.110
It was nothing but a distraction.

00:21:01.780 --> 00:21:06.660
All she needed was to buy enough time to pull off the second case.

00:21:07.410 --> 00:21:11.830
It was less a planned crime than a lucky coincidence.

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:19.500
She'd planned to kill Kanami, but hadn't planned
the rest of it in any detail until the earthquake happened.

00:21:22.050 --> 00:21:24.420
And then Shinya's called.

00:21:25.180 --> 00:21:28.470
He spoke to Akane, not Kanami.

00:21:30.180 --> 00:21:33.520
And Akane killed Kanami.

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:41.530
Shinya told us that Kanami had said something
about paint spilling, but that was a trick, too.

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:46.780
He phrased things ambiguously so we
wouldn't suspect him when we figured it out.

00:21:47.240 --> 00:21:48.780
It certainly fooled me.

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:50.990
Pure coincidence.

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:51.700
Was it?

00:21:52.240 --> 00:21:55.370
Seems statistically unlikely.

00:21:55.870 --> 00:21:57.580
But I'll take your word for it.

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:05.170
Anyway, she then created the locked room.
By deliberately spilling paint on the floor.

00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:12.680
So we were absolutely right to suspect Sonoyama at the time.

00:22:13.180 --> 00:22:14.810
That's right, Ilia.

00:22:15.350 --> 00:22:20.190
But because she'd made the locked room, we couldn't be sure.

00:22:20.730 --> 00:22:22.690
That's <i>why</i> she made it.

00:22:23.690 --> 00:22:26.890
She needed to be the right kind of suspect;

00:22:26.890 --> 00:22:35.290
she made the locked room so she would be suspicious, but not suspicious enough we'd be sure.

00:22:35.830 --> 00:22:38.080
So we'd lock her in the storeroom.

00:22:39.960 --> 00:22:45.960
But wait. Something doesn't make sense. Something's bothering me.

00:22:46.340 --> 00:22:51.220
Most likely...how did Akane get out of the storeroom?

00:22:51.430 --> 00:22:56.020
Yes! That! That's it! You haven't explained that!

00:22:56.640 --> 00:23:01.600
Did Shinya pull her out? When he was dropping the body off?

00:23:01.860 --> 00:23:08.190
No. Shinya only left the mansion to bury Kanami's body.

00:23:08.780 --> 00:23:14.280
I'm sure he shoved the body in the storeroom
window then, but didn't help Akane out.

00:23:14.780 --> 00:23:17.750
Hikari saw Akane still in the room at two AM.

00:23:18.460 --> 00:23:21.620
And Shinya has an all-night alibi.

00:23:22.460 --> 00:23:27.840
So Shinya couldn't have pulled her out. That much is certain.

00:23:28.260 --> 00:23:33.180
Then did he leave...maybe a rope ladder for her?

00:23:33.180 --> 00:23:39.770
No. It would have left marks. Maybe with a really long rope...

00:23:40.390 --> 00:23:44.270
But at two AM, Hikari saw the window closed.

00:23:44.730 --> 00:23:49.740
From inside the storeroom, there's no way Akane
could have attached a rope to something outside.

00:23:50.490 --> 00:23:59.040
Not without an accomplice; but like I said, her accomplice,
Shinya, was busy making an alibi with Maki.

00:23:59.450 --> 00:24:01.870
Then it seems impossible.

00:24:02.290 --> 00:24:05.420
Argh...my head's spinning.

00:24:05.790 --> 00:24:10.550
You're locked in. The door is locked from the outside.

00:24:10.880 --> 00:24:16.810
There's a window high up that you can open
as you please, and you want to get out of it.

00:24:17.470 --> 00:24:20.390
Ilia, in that situation, what would you do?

00:24:20.390 --> 00:24:23.100
I would never be in such a situation.

00:24:23.100 --> 00:24:25.940
Then...Akari, what about you?

00:24:26.270 --> 00:24:27.520
Me? Well...

00:24:28.610 --> 00:24:32.070
Yeah, I'd reach up my arms and jump.

00:24:32.320 --> 00:24:34.570
But you can't jump high enough.

00:24:34.990 --> 00:24:41.080
Then I'd try standing on a chair. And
then reaching up and jumping from there.

00:24:41.410 --> 00:24:45.380
But you still can't reach. What now? It's simple.

00:24:46.130 --> 00:24:49.130
You just need a higher chair.

00:24:49.130 --> 00:24:51.710
There was only one chair in that room.

00:24:52.220 --> 00:24:53.840
A metaphorical chair.

00:24:54.590 --> 00:24:56.800
Anything that could function like a chair.

00:24:57.300 --> 00:25:00.930
So...what else was in that room?

00:25:01.310 --> 00:25:02.430
Nothing.

00:25:02.980 --> 00:25:03.730
A book?

00:25:04.310 --> 00:25:05.730
Or the futon?

00:25:06.310 --> 00:25:07.730
Maybe the light?

00:25:08.190 --> 00:25:09.520
One more thing.

00:25:10.280 --> 00:25:11.990
We all saw it.

00:25:12.610 --> 00:25:15.110
We hardly looked at anything else.

00:25:15.490 --> 00:25:18.030
Ibuki's body, you mean.

00:25:19.450 --> 00:25:20.330
Yes.

00:25:21.080 --> 00:25:23.580
Rigor mortis peaks at 24 hours.

00:25:24.290 --> 00:25:26.080
With some variation.

00:25:26.460 --> 00:25:31.300
But at 2 AM, that body was most likely very stiff.

00:25:32.510 --> 00:25:36.470
I arrived at this idea while trying
to figure out why they cut off the head.

00:25:37.390 --> 00:25:41.720
Of course, the main reason was so they
could have Kanami's body play two roles.

00:25:41.720 --> 00:25:44.730
Blot this alll of

00:25:41.720 --> 00:25:44.730
4444

00:25:41.720 --> 00:25:44.730
Another line

00:25:41.720 --> 00:25:44.730
<i>Killer</i>

00:25:42.180 --> 00:25:44.020
Her face would prevent that.

00:25:44.980 --> 00:25:48.980
But I'm certain there was another reason.

00:25:49.650 --> 00:25:54.360
I doubt anyone else has ever cut
someone's head off for something like this.

00:25:56.490 --> 00:25:59.780
Namely...to create a level area above the shoulders.

00:26:01.330 --> 00:26:06.660
You mean...if it wasn't flat, she couldn't stand on it?

00:26:07.670 --> 00:26:10.040
It wouldn't be stable enough?

00:26:11.130 --> 00:26:14.010
Is that what you're saying?

00:26:14.340 --> 00:26:15.130
Yes.

00:26:15.760 --> 00:26:18.890
The body essentially functioned as a step.

00:26:19.470 --> 00:26:24.020
First, she placed the chair. Then she stood Kanami's body next to it.

00:26:24.640 --> 00:26:29.900
Then she jumped. First to the chair, then to Kanami's shoulders...

00:26:30.690 --> 00:26:33.570
Hop, step, jump.

00:26:34.320 --> 00:26:37.360
Then reached out her arms and caught the window.

00:26:38.360 --> 00:26:39.410
That's...

00:26:40.110 --> 00:26:44.700
That's too horrible. Too horrible. This is unforgivable.

00:26:45.370 --> 00:26:52.670
Killing someone, cutting off their head, burying them, digging
them back up, and disguising them as someone else...

00:26:53.630 --> 00:26:55.420
All that is horrible enough.

00:26:56.260 --> 00:26:57.800
Then to use them as a chair?

00:26:58.300 --> 00:26:59.430
As a stair?

00:27:00.090 --> 00:27:02.300
As a god damn stepping stone!?

00:27:02.970 --> 00:27:05.560
How can something like this...

00:27:08.640 --> 00:27:13.190
A headless corpse, reused as your own corpse.

00:27:14.110 --> 00:27:17.940
A headless corprse, used as a stepping stone.

00:27:18.860 --> 00:27:20.490
So what?

00:27:21.450 --> 00:27:22.620
Death was the end.

00:27:23.030 --> 00:27:24.780
They weren't coming back.

00:27:25.700 --> 00:27:29.210
That was all there was to it.

00:27:30.960 --> 00:27:32.880
That's all, Ilia.

00:27:33.330 --> 00:27:37.170
I can't be bothered explaining the details, so work them out yourself.

00:27:37.710 --> 00:27:41.510
Anything else is largely unimportant.

00:27:41.840 --> 00:27:43.010
The 'details'?

00:27:44.680 --> 00:27:46.010
What about the motive?

00:27:46.350 --> 00:27:50.560
That's not exactly what I call a 'detail'.

00:27:50.560 --> 00:27:52.650
You'd have to ask her.

00:28:05.160 --> 00:28:08.160
No need for you to answer, Shinya.

00:28:08.580 --> 00:28:09.660
Akane.

00:28:10.620 --> 00:28:11.410
My motive?

00:28:11.910 --> 00:28:15.210
Don't be absurd. What use is a motive?

00:28:15.500 --> 00:28:20.670
I can't comprehend giving a damn about
an insignificant, mundane little detail like that.

00:28:21.010 --> 00:28:24.930
Like there's anything to it beyond a slight difference of opinion.

00:28:26.760 --> 00:28:31.560
I just wanted to eat your brains.

00:28:38.020 --> 00:28:43.530
The shape of the world I'd believed in

00:28:43.530 --> 00:28:46.950
Spun around when near you

00:28:47.080 --> 00:28:50.290
Leaning towards your right

00:28:50.290 --> 00:28:52.790
What I've got in my hands

00:28:52.790 --> 00:28:55.630
Is not a dream or nothing

00:28:55.630 --> 00:28:59.300
But there's something somewhere

00:28:59.300 --> 00:29:02.340
Throbbing in my heart

00:29:02.340 --> 00:29:05.260
If the one that you do love

00:29:05.260 --> 00:29:09.640
Agrees to put his arms around you

00:29:09.640 --> 00:29:12.350
Then what was a nebulous hope

00:29:12.350 --> 00:29:16.600
Shatters everything that kept you stable

00:29:16.600 --> 00:29:19.190
We'd once been so hollow

00:29:19.190 --> 00:29:22.030
Trapped inside that little box

00:29:22.030 --> 00:29:25.530
But now we've seen outside that box

00:29:25.530 --> 00:29:28.780
And have no idea where we are.

00:29:29.200 --> 00:29:30.660
That's all.

00:29:44.550 --> 00:29:47.010
Afterimages of our bliss

00:29:47.010 --> 00:29:49.850
Glimpses of the future

00:29:49.850 --> 00:29:53.430
A glance at something fragile

00:29:53.430 --> 00:29:58.270
Those times that we can still laugh together
